<item><title>Niamey requires vacuum trucks to register and pay an annual fee</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niamey-requires-vacuum-trucks-to-register-and-pay-an-annual-b2b02d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niamey-requires-vacuum-trucks-to-register-and-pay-an-annual-b2b02d/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>Owners must register by 31 December 2026 and pay 20 CFA000 per truck from 1 January 2027.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:05:05 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Algerian military escort brings first fuel convoy into Niger</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/algerian-military-escort-brings-first-fuel-convoy-into-niger-a2f03a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/algerian-military-escort-brings-first-fuel-convoy-into-niger-a2f03a/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>The convoy was headed to Agadez after Algeria&apos;s parliament voted to send military units to protect energy interests.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:23:16 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/algerian-military-escort-brings-first-fuel-convoy-into-niger-a2f03a/share.jpg" length="41002" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/algerian-military-escort-brings-first-fuel-convoy-into-niger-a2f03a/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Gamkalé forage sellers get 50 francs CFA per bundle as water hyacinth spreads</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/gamkale-forage-sellers-get-50-francs-cfa-per-bundle-as-cbb5fc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/gamkale-forage-sellers-get-50-francs-cfa-per-bundle-as-cbb5fc/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>Sellers buy each bundle from children for 50 francs CFA and resell it for 100 francs, but an invasive plant is thinning demand.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:32:57 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Niamey growers seek flood barriers and cheaper farm inputs</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niamey-growers-seek-flood-barriers-and-cheaper-farm-inputs-9c1182/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ne/niamey-growers-seek-flood-barriers-and-cheaper-farm-inputs-9c1182/</guid><category>Niger</category><description>Gamkallé vegetable farmers say recurring floods and rising costs for seeds, manure and irrigation fuel are disrupting production.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:38:23 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" length="31036" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/ne.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
